apt 2.7.14 cmake: make XXHASH include dir project-wide

apt-pkg/pkgcachegen.h is a public header (installed under
include/apt-pkg/) and does `#include <xxhash.h>`.  The
XXHASH_INCLUDE_DIRS were only added to the apt-pkg target as PRIVATE
include dirs (apt-pkg/CMakeLists.txt), so consumers of the library
headers (e.g. apt-private/private-source.cc includes
apt-pkg/deblistparser.h -> apt-pkg/pkgcachegen.h) do not get the xxhash
include path.  On a distro Linux build /usr/include happens to hold
xxhash.h, so the bug is invisible; on a cross build (OHOS) the conan
prefix include dir is not in the compiler's default search path and the
build fails with:

  apt-private/private-source.cc:32: In file included from
  .../build-ohos/include/apt-pkg/deblistparser.h:15:
  .../include/apt-pkg/pkgcachegen.h:33:10: fatal error: 'xxhash.h' file not found

Fix by propagating XXHASH_INCLUDE_DIRS at top level so every target that
compiles apt-pkg public headers sees the include dir, mirroring what the
system /usr/include layout gives on Linux.

This is a portability fix for cross compilation; it has no effect on
Linux builds where XXHASH_INCLUDE_DIRS is empty or already in the
default search path.
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -142,6 +142,9 @@
 
 find_package(GCRYPT REQUIRED)
 find_package(XXHASH REQUIRED)
+if (XXHASH_FOUND)
+  include_directories(${XXHASH_INCLUDE_DIRS})
+endif()
 
 # Mount()ing and stat()ing and friends
 check_symbol_exists(statfs sys/vfs.h HAVE_VFS_H)

